WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:16.180
A shock wave of magic energy knocked Zann upward.

2
00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:21.323
He felt himself bump against the stalactite and slam against the cave's ceiling.

3
00:00:21.344 --> 00:00:23.305
"Ow!" He grunted.

4
00:00:24.346 --> 00:00:26.727
He twisted around and hugged the stalactite.

5
00:00:27.428 --> 00:00:32.171
His hand found a deep crack to hold onto, and he settled his feet on a small bump

6
00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:33.832
near the bottom of the stalactite.

7
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.742
Feeling secure, he sighed with relief.

8
00:00:37.482 --> 00:00:38.883
Then he untied the rope.

9
00:00:38.903 --> 00:00:41.285
"Careful, boy!"

10
00:00:41.685 --> 00:00:42.626
Wyssa called up to him.

11
00:00:43.466 --> 00:00:44.967
Zann lowered the rope to Wyssa.

12
00:00:46.828 --> 00:00:50.010
She grabbed it, gave it a tug, and yelled, "I'm ready!"

13
00:00:50.751 --> 00:00:54.493
The nomads yanked the rope, and Wyssa was lifted off the boulder.

14
00:00:55.274 --> 00:01:00.437
She swung over the cave hissers, kicking furiously as claws snapped at her feet.

15
00:01:01.198 --> 00:01:03.860
Up and up she went until she reached the top.

16
00:01:04.576 --> 00:01:06.237
Two nomads pulled her to safety.

17
00:01:07.097 --> 00:01:09.438
Next a nomad threw the rope back to Zann.

18
00:01:10.198 --> 00:01:13.940
He caught it with one hand while still gripping the stalactite with the other.

19
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.381
Zann breathed deeply.

20
00:01:17.341 --> 00:01:21.463
He let go of the stalactite and quickly grasped the rope with both hands.

21
00:01:22.223 --> 00:01:23.984
Immediately he swung downward.

22
00:01:24.964 --> 00:01:28.306
He used his feet to brace himself as he slammed into the wall.

23
00:01:28.326 --> 00:01:30.307
"Oof!" he cried.

24
00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:34.805
Soon he felt himself being raised up and out of the pit.

25
00:01:34.825 --> 00:01:40.327
"Wow!" Perda exclaimed as a nomad helped Zann onto the ledge.

26
00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:43.349
"I can't believe that worked."

27
00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:47.391
"Your bravery is inspiring, young man," the nomad said.

28
00:01:47.411 --> 00:01:53.855
"Yes, well Wyssa brushed off her clothes and shot Zann a grumpy look.

29
00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:57.316
"I suppose you did save my hide, boy.

30
00:01:57.737 --> 00:02:01.078
It's about time you repaid me for all the times I've saved yours."

31
00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:02.619
"You're welcome."

32
00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:03.740
Zann grinned.

33
00:02:04.492 --> 00:02:05.793
But then his grin faded.

34
00:02:05.813 --> 00:02:07.314
"What happened to Gliss?"

35
00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:09.355
Wyssa glanced around.

36
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:11.716
"I assumed she was with you."

37
00:02:11.736 --> 00:02:15.458
"The others are still searching," a nomad said.

38
00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:17.119
"We should join them."

39
00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:18.680
"I can help."

40
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.082
Wyssa pulled a handful of purple berries from her pocket.

41
00:02:22.102 --> 00:02:23.722
"Are those oogberries?"

42
00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:24.703
Zann asked.

43
00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:26.524
Wyssa didn't answer.

44
00:02:27.244 --> 00:02:30.486
She crushed the berries and then rubbed them onto her fingers.

45
00:02:30.506 --> 00:02:33.728
"This way," she said, exiting the cave.

46
00:02:35.048 --> 00:02:35.968
"What are you doing?"

47
00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.529
one of the nomads asked.

48
00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:40.350
"Is that magic from another world?"

49
00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.231
"Yes. It senses magical sources."

50
00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.071
Wyssa headed toward one of the hoof beasts.

51
00:02:47.952 --> 00:02:50.812
"Someone help me mount this creature, and I'll lead the way."

52
00:02:52.453 --> 00:02:54.793
Soon they were all riding across the desert.

53
00:02:55.594 --> 00:02:59.115
Wyssa was in the lead, occasionally changing direction slightly.

54
00:03:00.115 --> 00:03:02.356
"Are you sure you're following the right energy?"

55
00:03:02.836 --> 00:03:03.716
a nomad asked.

56
00:03:04.556 --> 00:03:05.516
He sounded nervous.

57
00:03:06.737 --> 00:03:10.178
When Zann looked around, all the nomads looked rather grim.

58
00:03:10.198 --> 00:03:11.859
"What's the matter?"

59
00:03:12.179 --> 00:03:12.800
Perda asked.

60
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.341
The nomads exchanged a look.

61
00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.582
"We're heading toward the Seeing Stone," one said.

62
00:03:18.602 --> 00:03:21.203
"That's where Morb was last seen."

63
00:03:22.244 --> 00:03:23.304
Zann looked at Wyssa.

64
00:03:24.004 --> 00:03:27.226
"Do you think your spell is leading us toward Morb instead of Gliss?"

65
00:03:27.246 --> 00:03:29.987
"It's possible," Wyssa said.

66
00:03:30.007 --> 00:03:32.088
"But we need to be sure.

67
00:03:32.936 --> 00:03:35.537
Unless you wish to abandon your friend out of fear?"

68
00:03:35.557 --> 00:03:37.817
"Of course not," Zann said.

69
00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:40.378
One nomad soon called for a halt.

70
00:03:40.398 --> 00:03:44.579
"We're definitely nearing the Seeing Stone," he whispered.

71
00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:46.920
"We should proceed with caution."

72
00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.441
Everyone dismounted the hoof beasts and tiptoed past some outcropping.

73
00:03:53.462 --> 00:03:55.382
Zann spotted the Seeing Stone immediately.

74
00:03:56.122 --> 00:04:01.604
It was a huge stone plateau with gently slopping sides and a flat, wide top.

75
00:04:02.396 --> 00:04:04.957
No wonder the nomads used it to view long distances.

76
00:04:05.657 --> 00:04:07.358
But he wasn't really thinking about that.

77
00:04:08.098 --> 00:04:11.220
He was focused on the ugly contraption standing in the middle.

78
00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.541
"Look!" Perda whispered.

79
00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:16.042
"It's one of Morb's contraptions!"

80
00:04:17.082 --> 00:04:17.822
Zann nodded.

81
00:04:18.503 --> 00:04:25.506
The contraption was an awkward jumble of bones, stones, and other things Zann couldn't recognize from this distance.

82
00:04:26.306 --> 00:04:31.168
It was smaller than some of the villain's previous contraptions, but it looked just as evil.

83
00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:34.566
"I don't see the girl," Wyssa murmured.

84
00:04:34.586 --> 00:04:38.749
"The spell locked onto the magic energy coming from Morb's contraption."

85
00:04:38.769 --> 00:04:41.371
"So how will we find Gliss?"

86
00:04:41.611 --> 00:04:42.151
Darb said.

87
00:04:42.171 --> 00:04:46.114
"We'll have to move away from here and try again," Perda said.

88
00:04:46.134 --> 00:04:51.818
"Maybe once we're away from that thing—" "We're not going anywhere yet," Wyssa said.

89
00:04:51.838 --> 00:04:55.780
"We must destroy it before Morb returns to finish it."

90
00:04:56.661 --> 00:04:58.282
"How can you tell it's not finished yet?"

91
00:04:58.923 --> 00:05:00.704
Zann glanced at the contraption again.

92
00:05:01.556 --> 00:05:03.397
"Is it because it's smaller than the other ones?"

93
00:05:03.417 --> 00:05:06.038
"That, and other reasons."

94
00:05:06.999 --> 00:05:08.000
Wyssa stepped forward.

95
00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.280
"Come with me.

96
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.621
We're going to need a lot of friction."

97
00:05:11.641 --> 00:05:13.703
"But what about Gliss?"

98
00:05:13.983 --> 00:05:14.503
Darb said.

99
00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:18.125
"We'll continue looking for Gliss soon," Wyssa said.

100
00:05:18.145 --> 00:05:20.566
"First we must stop Morb."

101
00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.567
"But—," Perda began.

102
00:05:23.348 --> 00:05:25.089
Wyssa was already walking away.

103
00:05:26.029 --> 00:05:27.690
Zann and his friends traded a glance.

104
00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.132
"I don't think we have a choice right now," Zann said.

105
00:05:32.276 --> 00:05:33.637
They all hurried after Wyssa.

106
00:05:35.338 --> 00:05:39.500
Zann, Perda, and the nomads rubbed their hands together to create magic friction.

107
00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.122
Finally Zann felt their energy sparking and buzzing around them.

108
00:05:44.903 --> 00:05:47.584
Meanwhile Wyssa had climbed atop the plateau.

109
00:05:47.604 --> 00:05:49.465
"Send it to me!"

110
00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:51.686
she called, rubbing her hands together.

111
00:05:52.707 --> 00:05:54.848
They sent all the energy up toward her.

112
00:05:55.508 --> 00:06:00.531
She held out her arms, and when the energy reached her, it burst into an enormous fireball.

113
00:06:00.551 --> 00:06:02.944
"Wow," Perda said.

114
00:06:03.865 --> 00:06:07.147
Wyssa lifted the fireball and turned toward the contraption.

115
00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:09.089
Zann held his breath.

116
00:06:09.849 --> 00:06:12.431
But then the old woman glanced down.

117
00:06:13.392 --> 00:06:15.453
Giant beetles were swarming toward her.

118
00:06:15.473 --> 00:06:17.755
"Darb, what are those things?"

119
00:06:18.175 --> 00:06:18.796
Zann asked.

120
00:06:18.816 --> 00:06:21.878
"I don't recognize them," Darb said.

121
00:06:21.898 --> 00:06:24.360
"They don't look very aggressive though."

122
00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:29.964
The beetles marched in tidy lines, clicking their antennae in time to their steps.

123
00:06:31.184 --> 00:06:34.327
Zann glanced at Wyssa, who was still gaping at the beetles.

124
00:06:35.147 --> 00:06:37.509
The fireball was beginning to fizzle out.

125
00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:39.531
"Quick!" Zann cried.

126
00:06:39.551 --> 00:06:41.753
"We have to send more energy up to Wyssa!"

127
00:06:42.613 --> 00:06:45.496
He and the others furiously rubbed their hands together again.

128
00:06:46.296 --> 00:06:50.780
But before they could get enough energy sparking, the fireball had disappeared.

129
00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.664
A second later Wyssa snapped her fingers and zapped out of sight.
